⁄ïJ”ˇDÜ∞{"url":"/gcsl/getting-started/running-a-first-program/","fragment":{"page_number":0,"data":{"url":"/gcsl/getting-started/running-a-first-program/","content":"Running a First Program. You can run a single GCSL file without creating a workspace. This example checks a small configuration and prints its computed description. Before you start # You need the following: The gcsl executable on your command search path. A writable directory for the example file. Create and run the file # Save the following text as hello.gcsl: Copylet component = {name = \"gcsl\"; version = \"0.1.0\"} \"{component.name} {component.version}\" Check the file without running it: Copygcsl check hello.gcsl Run the file: Copygcsl run hello.gcsl Check the result # The check reports no problems in 1 file checked on standard error. The run prints the string contents on standard output: Copygcsl 0.1.0 A file whose result is {}, the empty record, prints nothing. Diagnostics go to standard error. See gcsl(1) for exit statuses and output modes. Trying expressions interactively # Run gcsl without arguments to open the REPL. Enter let n = 21, then n * 2 on the next line. The second line prints 42 : Int. Each input is one line; separate several items on that line with semicolons. Press Ctrl+D to leave the session.","word_count":189,"filters":{},"meta":{"crumbs":"GCSL / Getting Started","title":"Running a First Program"},"anchors":[{"element":"h2","id":"before-you-start","text":"Before you start #","location":26},{"element":"h2","id":"create-and-run-the-file","text":"Create and run the file #","location":49},{"element":"h2","id":"check-the-result","text":"Check the result #","location":87},{"element":"h2","id":"trying-expressions-interactively","text":"Trying expressions interactively #","location":138}]}},"word_data":{"that":[{"position":179,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"21":[{"position":154,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"a":[{"position":1,"weight":168,"original_word":null},{"position"